ghost-role-information-tti-rules =
    You are [color={ role-type-crew-aligned-alternate-color }][bold]{ role-type-crew-aligned-name }[/bold][/color]. Locate the assigned patient, stabilize them and arrange medical evacuation.
    Coordinate with the medical department and security. An arrest does not authorize a jailbreak or an attack on security. Treat detained patients under security supervision.
    Use weapons only against an immediate attack. Do not seek revenge, pursue the patient's enemies or take part in a struggle for control of the station.
    Do not give weapons, armor or service equipment to the patient or crew. Use medical supplies for treatment. You may help other casualties if this does not prevent the evacuation.
    Leave aboard your shuttle after handing the patient over to medical staff or completing the evacuation. If rescue is impossible, report it and end the mission.
    You do not remember your previous life or anything learned as a ghost. General game knowledge is permitted; your previous character's identity and experiences are not.
